module effect_decl.neg_1

// `type X effect { fn op(..) -> T }` -- the declaration reads (2026-09-21)
// and is refused BY NAME, not by a lie.
//
// WHY THIS FIXTURE. Until the fix, `effect` fell into the alias tail
// (`type Name Y`, `effect` read as an ordinary type name) and the refusal
// was "undeclared type name `effect`" -- a misspelling nobody made, about
// an import nobody was missing. `effect` is a genuine word of the language
// (D61/D459), and this fixture pins the HONEST text so a regression of
// `check/check.nv`'s `@report_if_effect_type` or of the parser's
// `EFFECT_MARKER` arm in `parse/type_decl.nv` silently falls back to the
// wrong message rather than staying silent.
//
// THE SUBSTRING PINNED IS THE DISTINGUISHING PART, not the whole sentence
// (check-novac-fixture-expect.sh's own contract): "declares an effect" is
// specific to this refusal and cannot be produced by the old alias-tail
// path, which named `effect` itself as the undeclared thing.

// NOVAC_EXPECT declares an effect

type Counter effect {
    fn log(msg str) -> ()
}

fn main() {
    println(1)
}
